	(text "OOMWOO Hall sensor board (rev 1, 2026-10-28). One design, fitted twice: dust bin present (magnet in the bin) and the\nLiDAR tower bumper (magnet in the tower cover). Omnipolar: either magnet pole works. OUT goes low with the magnet near;\nthe main board pulls OUT up (47k), so open-drain and push-pull outputs both work. It samples at ~20-45 Hz.\nRefs in the 6000s: each board has its own range."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0fccef13-4077-4b3f-8dbb-bdec7a43bdc9")
	)
	(text "J6001 to the main board HALL-BIN1 or\nHALL-TOWER1, pin 1 to pin 1:\n1 3.3 V, 2 OUT, 3 GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127.254 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6def22f5-ca27-4728-9cd1-1ddce8fdc7fd")
	)
	(text "Mounting: 1x M2 (pad to GND)"
